---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

/** Shown under the heading. Change it whenever the disclaimer changes. */
const lastUpdated = '5 November 2026';
---

<Layout title="disclaimer" description="Cueory is a study aid, not medical advice." noindex>
  <Prose>
    <h1>disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <h2>Study help, not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} exists to help nursing students learn and prepare for exams. Nothing on this site is medical, nursing
      or clinical advice, a diagnosis, or a treatment recommendation, and nothing here creates a clinician–patient
      relationship. It is not a substitute for your nursing program, your instructors, your textbooks, your facility's
      policies or the judgment of a licensed clinician.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong class="key-term">Never use {site.name} to make a decision about a real patient.</strong> In a real
      situation, follow your program's and facility's policies, the orders you are given and your scope of practice. In
      an emergency, call your local emergency number.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We review our content and we correct it when we learn it is wrong, but we can't promise it is complete, current or
      free of mistakes. Clinical guidance, drug information, normal ranges and exam blueprints change over time, and
      sources sometimes disagree. Where a lesson shows a notice that it is a sample or has not yet been reviewed, treat
      it that way. Always check important points against your current course materials and a trusted reference, and
      study with more than one source.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you spot something wrong, please use the "Flag or comment" button on that page. Reports are how we find and
      fix errors.
    </p>

    <h2>Exams</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to any nursing school, licensing board, testing
      organization or textbook publisher. Using this site does not guarantee a grade, a passing score or a license.
    </p>

    <h2>Visual anatomy</h2>
    <p>
      Three-dimensional anatomy models are simplified teaching models. Shapes, sizes and positions can differ from any
      real person, and the models are not for clinical planning or diagnosis. The source and license of each model are
      named where it appears.
    </p>

    <h2>Links and videos</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages link to or embed material from other sites, such as lesson videos. We don't control those sites and are
      not responsible for their content or their privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      You use {site.name} at your own risk. Our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a> describe the limits on our liability.
      Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
